      },
      "The official Claude Code hooks reference is at code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks. It covers event schemas, configuration options, JSON input/output formats, exit codes, and advanced features such as async, HTTP, prompt, and MCP tool hooks. For a first-time walkthrough, the companion hooks guide is the better starting point.\n\nOther results:\n\n- **Lifecycle:** The reference describes hooks as user-defined shell commands, HTTP endpoints, or LLM prompts that run at set points in a session.\n- **Configuration:** Hooks live in user settings (`~/.claude/settings.json`) or project settings (`.claude/settings.json`), per the older docs.docs.claude.com page.\n- **Exit codes:** Exit code 2 blocks a PreToolUse tool call and sends stderr to Claude. For PostToolUse, the tool has already run, so the stderr is only shown to Claude.\n- **Third-party mirrors:** Community pages such as the claude-craft and shanraisshan references are unofficial. Treat them as secondary and check details against the official page."
